<section id="ending">
  <h2>Ending the scenario</h2><p class="source-note">Page 22</p><p>When the <strong>final Grey Lady</strong> is revealed, resolve its scene and cost. Then count the protagonist’s remaining Spirit and consult the scenario’s <strong>Spirit Table</strong>.</p>
  <div class="grid-2"><div class="card"><h3>Spirit remains</h3><p>The ending is generally more hopeful, survivable, or ambiguous.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>0 Spirit</h3><p>The protagonist is doomed: dead, broken, mad, transformed, or subjected to some worse fate.</p></div></div>
  <p class="motto">The Spirit Table is a guide, not a cage. Change the ending when your story clearly demands something else.</p>
</section>

<section id="reference">
  <h2>One-glance table reference</h2><p class="source-note">Pages 18–22</p>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>When this happens…</th><th>Do this</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Start play</td><td>Reveal the top card and begin the Narrative Track.</td></tr><tr><td>Clue</td><td>Reveal something meaningful about the horror or mystery.</td></tr><tr><td>Secondary character harmed</td><td>Show another character suffering harm; no obstacle roll by default.</td></tr><tr><td>Character / Environment obstructs</td><td>Roll d10 against card number + revealed Grey Ladies.</td></tr><tr><td>Obstacle succeeds</td><td>Give the protagonist a beneficial outcome.</td></tr><tr><td>Obstacle fails</td><td>Lose 1 Spirit and introduce a new hindrance.</td></tr><tr><td>Spend Resolve before roll</td><td>+2 per Resolve spent.</td></tr><tr><td>Spend Resolve after roll</td><td>+1 per Resolve spent.</td></tr><tr><td>Grey Lady</td><td>Use next Tension Table entry; spend 1 Resolve or lose 1 Spirit; future obstacle targets rise by +1.</td></tr><tr><td>Two cards revealed</td><td>One day passes in the journal.</td></tr><tr><td>Final Grey Lady resolved</td><td>Consult the Spirit Table and narrate the ending.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</section>
